{
  "id": "reversal-learning",
  "term": "reversal learning",
  "definition": "Reversal learning is a learning situation in which a person or animal first learns different responses to two stimuli based on reward and punishment, and then must adjust when those reward values are switched. It reflects learning to change a response when what was previously rewarded becomes punished, and vice versa.",
